# SwiftPM's build output for `apps/setup-helper`.
.build/

# `.mcp.json` is tracked, not ignored. It is the Claude Code plugin's
# own MCP server declaration (see `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`), and
# points at the installed `polarize` binary through PATH, not an
# absolute path. A contributor who wants their own local MCP
# registration for testing should use `claude mcp add --scope local`
# instead of editing this file, to avoid colliding with it.
